\subsection{Cross-Controller Functional Correctness}

Across 12 scenarios (4 stateful, 8 stateless) $\times$ 30 trials each, all four stateful and six of eight stateless scenarios achieve F1\,=\,1.000. The two exceptions (\texttt{cpu\_flicker\_01}, \texttt{ambiguous\_01}) yield F1\,=\,0.000 under both the proposed system and the No-FSM baseline---both present sub-threshold signals that neither controller dispatches, reflecting a shared signal-model limitation rather than a controller divergence.

